  <div class="tool-body">
    <div class="tool-in">
      <ol class="quiz"><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get coverage confirmed in writing. If the claim was denied, talk with an Ohio attorney before thinking about appraisal."><span>Has the insurer accepted coverage for at least part of the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Ask the adjuster for the complete itemized estimate in writing."><span>Do you have the insurer’s full line-item estimate, not just a payment letter?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get an independent line-item estimate; a one-page contractor bid won’t carry weight with a panel."><span>Do you have your own itemized estimate built from a site inspection?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Pull together every photo and note the date each one was taken."><span>Are there dated photos from right after the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Find the ‘Appraisal’ condition and note any appraiser-selection window."><span>Have you found and read the policy’s appraisal clause?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Calendar the suit-limitation date — many Ohio policies allow one year."><span>Do you know the date in the policy’s ‘Suit Against Us’ clause?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Make reasonable temporary repairs (tarps, water extraction) and keep every receipt."><span>Were temporary repairs made and receipts kept?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Make sure the full scope is visible before anyone puts a number on it."><span>Has hidden damage been opened up and documented — attic, wall cavities, basement?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Collect letters, emails and claim notes into one dated file."><span>Is the carrier correspondence saved in date order?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Run the claim gap & fee estimator — a small gap may not cover appraisal costs."><span>Is the gap more than roughly 10% of the insurer’s estimate or $5,000?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="btn-row"><button type="button" class="btn ghost small" data-reset>Clear answers</button></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-out tool-out-score" aria-live="polite">
      <div class="score-box">
        <svg class="gauge" viewBox="0 0 200 110" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#f1dfe1" stroke-width="18"/><path data-o="arc" d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#c12637" stroke-width="18" stroke-dasharray="251.3" stroke-dashoffset="251.3" style="transition:stroke-dashoffset .5s,stroke .3s"/></svg>
        <div class="gauge-num"><span data-o="score">–</span></div>
        <p class="hint" style="text-align:center">Answered <span data-o="count">0 / 10</span></p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="out-msg" data-o="verdict"></p>
        <p class="todo-h">Still to do</p>
        <ul data-o="todo" class="todo"></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div><noscript><p class="note-js">This calculator needs JavaScript. Turn it on, or call (844) 537-1427 and we’ll run the numbers with you.</p></noscript>
<p class="hint">For planning only. Results depend on what you enter and on your policy, and aren’t a quote, an appraisal or legal advice.</p></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>How the score is weighted</h2>
<p>Coverage, the two itemized estimates and early photos carry the most weight: without them appraisal is either the wrong tool or a weak one. Housekeeping items like organized correspondence still count, but they’re quicker to fix.</p>
<h2>What your number means</h2>
<ul><li><strong>75 or more:</strong> a solid file. The next step is a professional look at the dollar gap — see our <a href="/appraisal-practice/estimate-audit/">estimate audit</a>.</li>
<li><strong>45–74:</strong> work through the to-do list before demanding appraisal.</li>
<li><strong>Under 45:</strong> demanding now risks locking in a low award. Build the file first.</li></ul>
<h2>Questions about this tool</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Are my answers saved?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. The checkup runs in your browser and nothing is stored or sent.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does a high score mean I’ll win appraisal?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. It means your file has the pieces a panel expects. The award still depends on the evidence, the pricing and the people on the panel.</p></div></details><details><summary>What should I do if coverage was denied?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Appraisal generally decides the amount of a covered loss, not whether a loss is covered. For a denial, talk with an Ohio attorney.</p></div></details></div><h2>More free tools</h2><div class="rel-grid"><a class="rel" href="/appraisal-workbench/basement-backup-sublimit-calculator/"><small>Calculator</small><span>Basement Backup Sublimit Calculator</span><svg class="ar" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a class="rel" href="/appraisal-workbench/claim-gap-fee-estimator/"><small>Estimator</small><span>Claim Gap &amp; Fee Estimator</span><svg class="ar" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a class="rel" href="/appraisal-workbench/rcv-acv-holdback-calculator/"><small>Calculator</small><span>RCV/ACV Holdback Calculator</span><svg class="ar" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></article><aside class="side"><div class="side-box side-call"><h2 class="side-h">Talk it through first</h2><p>The first conversation is free. We’ll tell you plainly